championship in 1921. He was twice named to the all-state basketball team.
When Cohen graduated from high school, Alabama's baseball program was one of the best in the country.
Cohen had signed a baseball contract when he was 15 years old with Galveston of the Texas League but decided to abandon West Texas and head
to Alabama.
Cohen spent most of his time on the athletic fields at Alabama. He was a running back during football season,
a small quick guard in basketball and a second baseman on the baseball diamond.
